  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Low Density Polyethylene&nbsp;is obtained by the polymerisation of ethene under high pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>570</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> in the presence of an initiator. High Density Polyethylene&nbsp;is obtained when polymerisation is done in the presence of Ziegler-Natta catalyst at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>333</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>343</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> under <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure.&nbsp;Nylon-6 is manufactured from the monomer called caprolactam. The monomer caprolactam is heated at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>533</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>543</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>in an inert atmosphere, it polymerises to give nylon-6.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
